IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`

-- je54-art11-powers: Articles 11 and 11A of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, for a given TEXT of the Law.
-- Articles 11(1) and 11(2) are the same in all seven deposited texts.  Articles 11(3) and 11(4) are in V1 only (deleted by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 from 28 September 2021; the placeholders "(3) [12]" and
-- "(4) [13]" of the later texts are inert and are refused here).  Article 11A is in V2a to V2f only (inserted by the same Law, from 28 September 2021).  Selecting date: the day the power is exercised or the
-- appointment is made (the day the fact occurred); the caller reads the text for that day.  A question about a day before 1 January 2019 refuses (no text is deposited).
-- Article 11A says "unless the contrary is expressed", not "unless the contrary intention appears": a contrary intention that appears only by implication is not enough there.  The input is named for the words used.

§ `Article 11: Construction of provisions as to exercise of powers and duties`

-- src:50 | (1) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power or imposes a duty, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(1) (src:50)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(1): the enactment neither confers a power nor imposes a duty` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 11(1) deals only where an enactment confers a power or imposes a duty"

-- src:50 | (1) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power or imposes a duty, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(1) (src:50)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(1): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 11(1) does not say how often the power may be exercised or the duty performed"

-- 11(1): the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.  "As occasion requires" is the caller's judgement.  A power that has been exercised before may be exercised
-- again, and a duty that has been performed before must be performed again, whenever occasion requires.  Whether it has been used before is accepted and ignored: "from time to time" is the whole of the point.
-- src:50 | (1) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power or imposes a duty, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(1) (src:50)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment confers a power or imposes a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power or duty has been used or performed before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `occasion requires it again` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11(1): the power may be exercised or the duty must be performed on this occasion` v `the enactment confers a power or imposes a duty` `the power or duty has been used or performed before` `occasion requires it again` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `the enactment confers a power or imposes a duty` THEN `Article 11(1): the enactment neither confers a power nor imposes a duty`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 11(1): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE `occasion requires it again`

-- src:51 | (2) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the holder for the time being of the office, or, in case of his or her absence or incapacity, by the person for the time being performing the duty of that office.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(2) (src:51)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(2): the enactment does not confer the power or impose the duty on the holder of an office as such` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 11(2) deals only where an enactment confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such"

-- src:51 | (2) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the holder for the time being of the office, or, in case of his or her absence or incapacity, by the person for the time being performing the duty of that office.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(2) (src:51)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(2): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 11(2) does not say who exercises the power or performs the duty"

-- src:51 | (2) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the holder for the time being of the office, or, in case of his or her absence or incapacity, by the person for the time being performing the duty of that office.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(2) (src:51)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(2): nobody is performing the duty of the office` MEANS
    REFUSE "the holder of the office is absent or incapacitated and nobody is performing the duty of the office: Article 11(2) names no one"

-- 11(2): the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the holder for the time being of the office, or, in case of the holder's absence or incapacity, by the person for the time being performing the
-- duty of that office.  What counts as absence or incapacity, and whether anyone is "performing the duty", are the caller's facts.
-- src:51 | (2) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power or imposes a duty on the holder of an office as such, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed by the holder for the time being of the office, or, in case of his or her absence or incapacity, by the person for the time being performing the duty of that office.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(2) (src:51)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment confers the power or imposes the duty on the holder of an office as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      holder IS A STRING
      `the holder is absent or incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person for the time being performing the duty of the office` IS A MAYBE STRING
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`Article 11(2): who exercises the power or performs the duty of the office` v `the enactment confers the power or imposes the duty on the holder of an office as such` holder `the holder is absent or incapacitated` `the person for the time being performing the duty of the office` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `the enactment confers the power or imposes the duty on the holder of an office as such` THEN `Article 11(2): the enactment does not confer the power or impose the duty on the holder of an office as such`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 11(2): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           IF NOT `the holder is absent or incapacitated` THEN holder
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the person for the time being performing the duty of the office`
               WHEN NOTHING THEN `Article 11(2): nobody is performing the duty of the office`
               WHEN JUST performer THEN performer

-- 11(3) (V1 only): a power to pass any other enactment is construed as including a power, exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, rescind, amend or vary
-- that other enactment.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:52 | (3) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power to pass any other enactment, the power shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as including a power, exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, rescind, amend or vary that other enactment.
-- src:52 | (3) [12]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(3), as it read before 28 September 2021, and its placeholder in the later texts (src:l_17_1954_20210927:52), (src:52)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(3): deleted from 28 September 2021` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 11(3) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:52 | (3) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power to pass any other enactment, the power shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as including a power, exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, rescind, amend or vary that other enactment.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(3), as it read before 28 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:52)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(3): the enactment does not confer power to pass another enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 11(3) deals only where an enactment confers a power to pass any other enactment"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:52 | (3) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power to pass any other enactment, the power shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as including a power, exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, rescind, amend or vary that other enactment.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(3), as it read before 28 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:52)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(3): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 11(3) does not say what the power to pass the other enactment then includes"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:52 | (3) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power to pass any other enactment, the power shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as including a power, exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, rescind, amend or vary that other enactment.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(3), as it read before 28 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:52)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment confers a power to pass another enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS AN `Act on an enactment`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11(3): the power to pass the other enactment includes the power` v `the enactment confers a power to pass another enactment` act `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Article 11(3) and 11(4) are in the text` v THEN `Article 11(3): deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF NOT `the enactment confers a power to pass another enactment` THEN `Article 11(3): the enactment does not confer power to pass another enactment`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 11(3): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER act
               WHEN `to repeal it` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `to rescind it` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `to amend it` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `to vary it` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `some other act on it` THEN FALSE

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:52 | (3) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, confers a power to pass any other enactment, the power shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as including a power, exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions, if any, to repeal, rescind, amend or vary that other enactment.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:53 | (4) Where an enactment passed after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make any other enactment, the power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:54 | (a) either in relation to all cases to which the power extends, or in relation to all those cases subject to specified exceptions, or in relation to any specified cases or classes of case; and
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:55 | (b) so as to make, as respects the cases in relation to which it is exercised –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:56 | (i) the full provision to which the power extends or any lesser provision (whether by way of exception or otherwise),
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:57 | (ii) the same provision for all cases in relation to which the power is exercised, or different provision for different cases or classes of case, or different provision as respects the same case or class of case for different purposes of the enactment,
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:58 | (iii) any such provision either unconditionally or subject to any specified condition.[9]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(3) and 11(4) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:52-58)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11(3) and 11(4) are in the text` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `V1, 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 11(4) (V1 only): where an enactment passed after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make any other enactment, the power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised in the ways listed.
-- "After 28th March 2003" is read as a date: an enactment passed on 28 March 2003 itself was not passed after 28th March 2003.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:53 | (4) Where an enactment passed after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make any other enactment, the power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:54 | (a) either in relation to all cases to which the power extends, or in relation to all those cases subject to specified exceptions, or in relation to any specified cases or classes of case; and
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:55 | (b) so as to make, as respects the cases in relation to which it is exercised –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:56 | (i) the full provision to which the power extends or any lesser provision (whether by way of exception or otherwise),
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:57 | (ii) the same provision for all cases in relation to which the power is exercised, or different provision for different cases or classes of case, or different provision as respects the same case or class of case for different purposes of the enactment,
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:58 | (iii) any such provision either unconditionally or subject to any specified condition.[9]
-- src:53 | (4) [13]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(4), as it read before 28 September 2021, and its placeholder in the later texts (src:l_17_1954_20210927:53-58), (src:53)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(4): deleted from 28 September 2021` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 11(4) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:53 | (4) Where an enactment passed after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make any other enactment, the power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(4), as it read before 28 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:53)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(4): the enactment does not confer a power to make another enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 11(4) deals only where an enactment passed after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make any other enactment"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:53 | (4) Where an enactment passed after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make any other enactment, the power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(4), as it read before 28 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:53)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11(4): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 11(4) does not say how the power may then be exercised"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:53 | (4) Where an enactment passed after 28th March 2003 confers a power to make any other enactment, the power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:54 | (a) either in relation to all cases to which the power extends, or in relation to all those cases subject to specified exceptions, or in relation to any specified cases or classes of case; and
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:55 | (b) so as to make, as respects the cases in relation to which it is exercised –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:56 | (i) the full provision to which the power extends or any lesser provision (whether by way of exception or otherwise),
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:57 | (ii) the same provision for all cases in relation to which the power is exercised, or different provision for different cases or classes of case, or different provision as respects the same case or class of case for different purposes of the enactment,
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:58 | (iii) any such provision either unconditionally or subject to any specified condition.[9]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11(4), as it read before 28 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:53-58)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment confers a power to make another enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the enactment conferring the power was passed` IS A DATE
      way IS A `Way a power to make an enactment is exercised`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11(4): the power may be exercised in the way` v `the enactment confers a power to make another enactment` `the day on which the enactment conferring the power was passed` way `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Article 11(3) and 11(4) are in the text` v THEN `Article 11(4): deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF NOT `the enactment confers a power to make another enactment` THEN `Article 11(4): the enactment does not confer a power to make another enactment`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 11(4): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           IF NOT (`the day on which the enactment conferring the power was passed` GREATER THAN `the day on which the Interpretation (Amendment) (Jersey) Law 2003 came into force`) THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER way
               WHEN `in some other way` THEN FALSE
               OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `Article 11A: Power to appoint to an office includes related powers`

-- src:55 | (1) If an enactment confers power to appoint a person to an office, unless the contrary is expressed the power includes power –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11A(1) (src:55)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11A: inserted from 28 September 2021` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 11A of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is inserted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not in the text of the Law in force on this day"

-- src:55 | (1) If an enactment confers power to appoint a person to an office, unless the contrary is expressed the power includes power –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11A(1) (src:55)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11A: the enactment does not confer power to appoint a person to an office` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 11A deals only where an enactment confers power to appoint a person to an office"

-- src:55 | (1) If an enactment confers power to appoint a person to an office, unless the contrary is expressed the power includes power –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11A(1) (src:55)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 11A: the contrary is expressed, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "the contrary is expressed: Article 11A does not say what the power to appoint then includes"

-- src:55 | (1) If an enactment confers power to appoint a person to an office, unless the contrary is expressed the power includes power –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11A (src:55)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11A is in the text` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `V2a, 28 September 2021 to 30 January 2022` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2b, 31 January 2022 to 31 August 2022` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2c, 1 September 2022 to 10 January 2024` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2d, 11 January 2024 to 23 November 2025` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2e, 24 November 2025 to 18 June 2026` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `V2f, 19 June 2026 to current` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 11A(2): the circumstances in which 11A(1)(d) applies.
-- src:60 | (2) The circumstances for the purposes of paragraph (1)(d) are where –
-- src:61 | (a) the office is vacant;
-- src:62 | (b) the person holding the office has been removed or suspended from office;
-- src:63 | (c) the person holding the office is absent temporarily or permanently; or
-- src:64 | (d) the person holding the office is incapacitated temporarily or permanently in a way that affects the person’s performance.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11A(2) (src:60-64)
GIVEN c IS A `Circumstances of an office`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11A(2): the circumstances for the power to appoint in place of the last holder are met` c MEANS
        c's `the office is vacant`
     OR c's `the person holding the office has been removed or suspended from office`
     OR c's `the person holding the office is absent temporarily or permanently`
     OR c's `the person holding the office is incapacitated in a way that affects the person's performance`

-- 11A(1): unless the contrary is expressed, the power to appoint includes power (a) to determine terms and conditions, (b) to remove or suspend, (c) to reappoint or reinstate, and (d) in the circumstances in (2), to
-- appoint a person in place of the last holder.
-- src:55 | (1) If an enactment confers power to appoint a person to an office, unless the contrary is expressed the power includes power –
-- src:56 | (a) to determine the terms and conditions of appointment;
-- src:57 | (b) to remove or suspend a person from the office;
-- src:58 | (c) to reappoint or reinstate a person to the office; and
-- src:59 | (d) in the circumstances set out in paragraph (2), to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 11A(1) (src:55-59)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment confers power to appoint a person to an office` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `Power related to an appointment`
      c IS A `Circumstances of an office`
      `the contrary is expressed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 11A: the power to appoint to an office includes the power` v `the enactment confers power to appoint a person to an office` power c `the contrary is expressed` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Article 11A is in the text` v THEN `Article 11A: inserted from 28 September 2021`
           IF NOT `the enactment confers power to appoint a person to an office` THEN `Article 11A: the enactment does not confer power to appoint a person to an office`
           IF `the contrary is expressed` THEN `Article 11A: the contrary is expressed, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER power
               WHEN `to determine the terms and conditions of appointment` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `to remove or suspend a person from the office` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `to reappoint or reinstate a person to the office` THEN TRUE
               WHEN `to appoint a person to the office in place of the last holder of the office` THEN `Article 11A(2): the circumstances for the power to appoint in place of the last holder are met` c
               WHEN `some other power` THEN FALSE
